“Do you think he’s telling the truth?”
He said, “You have power while so many women are powerless.”
Flake said his department issued a statement and added that he had more to say at the Legal Affairs Committee's hearing before the elevator closed.
Cable distribution and broadcasting networks recorded live broadcasting several hours later, when the Committee on Legal Affairs had to vote to forward Kavanaugh's nomination for voting to the Senate Plenary.
But Flake said he's only doing this in the realization that the FBI is investigating accusations against the nominee next week that have been demanded by minority Democrats.
Flake was partially persuaded to have a conversation with his friend Democrat Senator Chris Coons.
After a later conversation with Coons and other senators, Flake made his decision.
