“Verifying Congress is so important for the president’s agenda that Trump travels to as many states as possible by diving into the busy election campaign season,” a Trump campaign spokesman told Reuters.
Tonight’s campaign, scheduled to take place at Wesbanco Stadium in Wheeling, could bring in supporters from “Ohio and Pennsylvania and get coverage in the Pittsburgh media as well.”
It's the second time Trump's visit to West Virginia over the past month on Saturday, a state where he received more than 40 percent of the vote in 2016.
Trump seeks to help West Virginia's Republican Senatician Patrick Morriesy, who is leading the rankings based on polls.
“It’s not a good sign for Morrisey that the president has come to encourage his results,” said Simon Haeder, a polithologist at the University of West Virginia.
Ryder Cup 2018: U.S. team will have enough nerve to compete, keeping hopes high before Sunday's solitary matches
After three one-sided sessions, the games that took place on Saturday afternoon were perhaps exactly what the Ryder Cup needed.
Fluctuating the pivotal pendulum is a completely fictional concept in sports, but players truly believe in it, especially in competitions like this one.
So, where do they think it's a turning point right now?
“They led by six points, which has now become four, so I think it can be considered a small turning point,” said Jordan Spieth at the end of the day.
Europe has an advantage, that's clear, as they're leading by four points and still having 12 points in the game.
Spieth said the Americans don't have enough breeze to sail, but they have a lot of encouragement, especially Spieth and Justin Thomas, who played together all day, and each got three points out of four.
Spieth has been stunning in the case of both women and greens and sets an example.
Those cries of victory from the throat became louder with each lap, overshadowing the defining stool that would have led to a tie for the fourth match after he and Thomas were on the ground with two.
