Europe has played better as a team so far and taken the lead for the last day with a strong lead, but this quartet session showed that the U.S. team has enough nerve to fight, in which some, especially the Americans, have doubted.
Europe takes 10-6 lead on the last day of the Ryder Cup
Europe will have a good lead on the last day of the Ryder Cup, taking a 10-6 lead over the United States after Saturday's four-balls and doubles.
Excellent duo Tommy Fleetwood and Francesco Molinari led Tiger Woods with two wins to raise their current scoring at Le Golf National to four points.
