He appeared in court on Saturday, declaring that he was “not guilty in any way,” the news network reported
Palin faces three class A misdemeanors, which means he could face up to a year in prison and a fine of US$250,000.
He has also been charged with class B misdemeanor punishable by a one-day captivity and a 2000-dollar fine.
This isn't the first time Palini has been charged.
In December 2017, he was accused of attacking his father, Todd Palin.
In connection with the alleged attack, his mother, Sarah Palin, was summoned by police.
The case is currently being heard in the Alaska Veteran Court.
In January 2016, he was accused of domestic assault, interfering in a report on domestic violence crime and possession of a weapon, all in a state of intoxication.
