Indonesia's tsunami: Hundreds killed
At least 384 people have been killed after an earthquake on the Indonesian island of Sulawesi on Friday.
A 7.5-degree earthquake triggered a tsunami and destroyed thousands of homes.
Electricity and communication networks are not functioning and the number of deaths is expected to increase in the coming days.
The quake hit the outskirts of downtown Sulawesi, northeastern of the Indonesian capital Jakarta.
There are videos circulating on social media showing the moment of the earthquake.
